The JavaScript marshalling checks in sdk/typescript/canonical.mjs adapt
src/canonical.ts from MetaMap 0.7.1, revision
399747a4ad05a37cd8db1cedd53048fad2175be4 (Apache-2.0, Rory Dahl).
Patamaps executes canonical encoding, strict parsing and hashing in Rust.

The read-only legacy graph validator in patamaps-core adapts the shape and
semantic validation contract from src/validator.ts at the same pinned
Apache-2.0 revision. Its reports cannot construct an admitted generation or
authorize a protected transaction.
legacy_core.json preserves the default core relation data exported by
src/relations.ts at that pinned revision, under the same license.
The native legacy CLI planner/renderer, its preserved usage text, and source
catalog migration adapt src/cli.ts and src/adapters/source-of-truth.ts at
that revision, under the same Apache-2.0 license. The compatibility entry
uses the Patamaps engine and optional fact providers.
The version-dispatched legacy pack importer interprets the preserved 1.0/2.0
relation-pack schemas from that revision. Original documents and digest
conventions remain separate from native draft views; importing confers no
admission or authorization. Executable dependency checking shares the native
law checker. Full original JavaScript registry behavior remains a parity target.

adapters/discovery extracts the Apache-2.0 Prisma, TypeScript/Zod, Next.js,
JSON collection, legacy catalog, SSSOM and portable-shard fact providers and their type/fact helpers
from the same pinned MetaMap revision. Its provenance.json identifies the
original source and compiled bytes and the limited declaration adaptations.
The shard wrapper's sole code relocation points to its unmodified bundled
graph schema; Ajv performs shape checking without reference semantic validation.
It includes no reference policy, admission, governance or graph compiler.
The SSSOM fact wrapper delegates its parser, interpretation, source schema
validation and canonical encoding to the Rust scientific engine. The fixed
scientific relation data retains its original license and versioned digest.

Consuming repositories remain responsible for their own graph documents,
correspondences, authority decisions, viability policies, and generated
projections. Those artifacts are not licensed by this NOTICE unless they
are published as part of this repository's examples.

The unmodified SSSOM 1.0.0 model and license are retained under
fixtures/reference/standards/sssom-1.0.0 (BSD-3-Clause). The MGI seven-record
producer subset retains its source-declared CC BY 4.0 license, creator IDs,
selection manifest and provenance under fixtures/reference/examples/scientific-mapping.
These source licenses are not replaced by this repository's code license.

The pinned RO-Crate 1.2 JSON-LD context is distributed by the Research Object
Crate contributors under CC0 1.0 Universal. Its exact bytes and source URL are
recorded in fixtures/scientific/ro-crate-context-pin.json. Upstream attribution:
https://github.com/ResearchObject/ro-crate#license

The preserved legacy URI-reference format pattern derives from ajv-formats
3.0.1 (dist/formats.js), used by the pinned MetaMap parser. Its ASCII
case/digit and regex-literal escapes are adapted for the native regex engine.
