The legacy graph query and shard composition interfaces adapt src/graph.ts and
src/composer.ts at the pinned Apache-2.0 MetaMap revision. Native Rust decides
legacy indexes, queries, equivalence, merge handles and conflicts; SDK handles
retain caller objects. These observations grant no admission or authorization.

The native legacy composer and unchecked legacy digests use the Unicode
Consortium's ICU4X icu_collator 2.2.1 with its locked compiled collation data.
The vendored copy adds a tagged UTF-16 comparison path for unpaired units;
only src/comparison.rs and src/elements.rs are patched, and the complete
vendored source is bound into the compiler identity. The patch and original
file inventory are documented in vendor/icu_collator/PATAMAPS-PATCH.md and
vendor/icu_collator/PATAMAPS-UPSTREAM.json. The upstream source is
https://github.com/unicode-org/icu4x and its API is documented at
https://docs.rs/icu_collator/2.2.1/icu_collator/struct.Collator.html .
The original runtime locale is an explicit observation input. Complete
collation-data equivalence across ICU versions/platforms remains unverified.
